        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): docs, help, Discord, and changelog links in the agent chip menu",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFollow-up to #105777/#105832: the footer agent-chip menu links only to Docs. Users have no in-product path to release notes, help, or the community — the places we route people to for \"what changed\" and \"I'm stuck\".\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTable-drives the menu's external rows and adds three links alongside Docs, docs-first per our public-copy policy: Get help (docs.openclaw.ai/help), Discord community (discord.gg/clawd, the canonical invite from the README), and View changelog (docs.openclaw.ai/releases). Same external-link handling (target/rel) and menu-close behavior as the existing Docs row.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe agent chip menu now answers \"what changed\" and \"where do I get help\" without leaving the product chrome: Docs, Get help, Discord community, View changelog.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Unit test asserts the exact href list rendered in the menu; 38/38 green on Blacksmith Testbox (Linux) plus `pnpm tsgo:ui`.\n- All three URLs verified live (docs pages return 200; discord.gg/clawd is the README's canonical invite).\n- Codex autoreview (gpt-5.5) on the isolated diff: clean.\n- Locale sync authenticated, fallbacks=0 across 20 bundles; keyless `ui:i18n:check` clean.\n",
